  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3309.07 Required Number of State Labels.\n\n(a) Each module of a modular building shall have a separate label.\n\n(b) Previously labeled modular buildings or building components that are relocated into the state, or within the state, shall be re-inspected and re-labeled by the department or agency pursuant to Saf-C 3310.05.\n\nSource. #5439, eff 7-24-92; amd by #5935, eff 12-20-94; ss by #6810, INTERIM, eff 7-25-98, EXPIRES: 11-22-98; ss by #6885, eff 11-18-98; ss by #8741, INTERIM, eff 11-18-06, EXPIRED: 5-17-07\n\nNew. #9752, eff 7-9-10 (from Saf-C 3309.05); ss by #12737, eff 3-8-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3300.html"
